<h1 style="text-align:center; font-size:18pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">DURABLE GENERAL POWER OF ATTORNEY</h1>
<p style="text-align:center; font-size:10pt; color:#555; margin-bottom:24pt;">
  State of New Jersey &mdash; Pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.1 <em>et seq.</em>
</p>

<p><strong>I, {{clientFullName}}</strong>, born on {{formatDate personalInfo.dob}}, residing at {{personalInfo.address}}, {{personalInfo.city}}, {{personalInfo.county}} County, New Jersey {{personalInfo.zip}}, being of sound mind, do hereby make, constitute, and appoint the following as my Attorney-in-Fact (hereinafter &ldquo;Agent&rdquo;):</p>

<h2>ARTICLE I &mdash; APPOINTMENT OF AGENT</h2>

<p><strong>1.1 Primary Agent:</strong> I appoint <strong>{{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent}}</strong>
{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.relationship}} ({{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.relationship}}){{/if}},
residing at {{fillOrBlank fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.address}},
as my Agent under this Power of Attorney.</p>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent}}
<p><strong>1.2 Alternate Agent:</strong> If my primary Agent is unable, unwilling, or ceases to serve for any reason, I appoint <strong>{{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent}}</strong>
{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent.relationship}} ({{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent.relationship}}){{/if}} as my alternate Agent with all the same powers and authority.</p>
{{/if}}

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent}}
<p><strong>1.3 Successor Agent:</strong> If both my primary and alternate Agents are unable, unwilling, or cease to serve, I appoint <strong>{{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent}}</strong>
{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent.relationship}} ({{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent.relationship}}){{/if}} as my successor Agent.</p>
{{/if}}

<h2>ARTICLE II &mdash; EFFECTIVE DATE AND DURABILITY</h2>

<p><strong>2.1 Effective Date.</strong> This Power of Attorney {{#if (eq fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.effectiveDate 'immediate')}}shall become effective immediately upon execution and shall remain in full force and effect unless revoked by me in writing{{else}}shall become effective only upon my incapacity or disability as certified in writing by my attending physician, and shall thereafter remain in full force and effect unless revoked by me in writing during a period of competency{{/if}}.</p>

<p><strong>2.2 Durability.</strong> This is a <u>durable</u> power of attorney. It shall not be affected by my subsequent disability or incapacity, pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.1. The authority of my Agent shall continue notwithstanding any subsequent uncertainty as to whether I am dead or alive.</p>

<h2>ARTICLE III &mdash; POWERS GRANTED</h2>

<p>I grant to my Agent full power and authority to act on my behalf in the following matters:</p>

<p><strong>3.1 Real Property Transactions.</strong> To lease, sell, exchange, mortgage, deed, convey, quitclaim, or otherwise encumber or dispose of any real property; to manage, maintain, improve, and insure real property; to pay or contest property taxes and assessments; to appear for me before any land use board or governmental agency.</p>

<p><strong>3.2 Banking and Financial Transactions.</strong> To open, close, and manage accounts at any financial institution; to make deposits and withdrawals; to negotiate, endorse, and deposit checks; to wire funds; to access safe deposit boxes; to establish and manage certificates of deposit, money market accounts, and investment accounts.</p>

<p><strong>3.3 Securities and Investment Transactions.</strong> To buy, sell, exchange, and trade in stocks, bonds, mutual funds, ETFs, and other securities; to exercise stock options; to manage margin accounts; to establish or modify brokerage accounts; to retain, hire, or discharge investment advisors.</p>

<p><strong>3.4 Business Operations.</strong> To form, operate, manage, and dissolve any business entity in which I have an interest; to execute contracts, agreements, and business documents; to hire and terminate employees; to buy and sell business assets; to exercise all rights as a member, partner, shareholder, or owner.</p>

<p><strong>3.5 Insurance and Annuity Transactions.</strong> To procure, maintain, modify, or cancel any insurance policies or annuity contracts; to designate or change beneficiaries (subject to applicable ERISA restrictions); to file and settle claims; to receive and apply insurance proceeds.</p>

<p><strong>3.6 Retirement Plan Transactions.</strong> To contribute to, withdraw from, or manage any retirement plan, IRA, 401(k), 403(b), pension, or annuity; to roll over or transfer retirement funds; to elect distribution options; to designate or change beneficiaries (subject to spousal consent requirements under ERISA where applicable).</p>

<p><strong>3.7 Tax Matters.</strong> To prepare, sign, and file federal, state, and local tax returns; to represent me before the IRS, NJ Division of Taxation, or any other taxing authority; to make elections and enter into agreements including installment agreements; to execute waivers, consents, and closing agreements; to receive and endorse tax refund checks.</p>

<p><strong>3.8 Claims and Litigation.</strong> To commence, prosecute, defend, or settle any legal action or administrative proceeding on my behalf; to retain and discharge attorneys; to submit to alternative dispute resolution; to execute settlements and releases; to satisfy judgments.</p>

<p><strong>3.9 Government Benefits.</strong> To apply for and manage government benefits including Social Security, Medicare, Medicaid, veterans&rsquo; benefits, and any other government program; to represent me before any government agency.</p>

<p><strong>3.10 Estate, Trust, and Beneficiary Transactions.</strong> To create, amend, or revoke trusts; to fund trusts with my assets; to disclaim inheritances; to exercise any power of appointment; to represent me in estate or trust administration.</p>

<p><strong>3.11 Personal and Family Maintenance.</strong> To provide for my support and maintenance and that of my dependents; to make decisions regarding my residence and living arrangements (excluding health care decisions); to manage household affairs.</p>

<p><strong>3.12 Digital Assets.</strong> To access, manage, and control my digital assets, including email accounts, social media accounts, online financial accounts, digital photographs and media, cryptocurrency, domain names, and any other digital property, pursuant to the Revised Uniform Fiduciary Access to Digital Assets Act (N.J.S.A. 3B:31-50 <em>et seq.</em>).</p>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.giftingPower}}
<h2>ARTICLE IV &mdash; GIFTING AUTHORITY</h2>

<p><strong>4.1</strong> My Agent is specifically authorized to make gifts of my property, including gifts to the Agent personally, in accordance with the following provisions and pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.13a:</p>

<p>(a) Gifts shall not exceed the annual federal gift tax exclusion amount per donee per calendar year;</p>
<p>(b) Gifts shall be consistent with my established pattern of giving;</p>
<p>(c) Gifts may include contributions to 529 college savings plans for my grandchildren or other descendants;</p>
<p>(d) The aggregate of all gifts in any calendar year shall not reduce my estate below an amount sufficient for my care, maintenance, and support.</p>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.selfDealingPower}}
<p><strong>4.2 Self-Dealing.</strong> My Agent is authorized to engage in self-dealing transactions, including making gifts to himself or herself, provided such transactions are consistent with my expressed wishes and prior gifting patterns.</p>
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.limitations}}
<h2>ARTICLE {{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.giftingPower}}V{{else}}IV{{/if}} &mdash; LIMITATIONS</h2>
<p>Notwithstanding any other provision of this Power of Attorney, the following limitations apply:</p>
<p>{{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.limitations}}</p>
{{/if}}

<h2>GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>

<p><strong>Compensation.</strong> My Agent shall be entitled to reasonable compensation for services rendered under this Power of Attorney, plus reimbursement of all reasonable out-of-pocket expenses incurred in the performance of Agent&rsquo;s duties.</p>

<p><strong>Accounting.</strong> My Agent shall maintain accurate records of all transactions made on my behalf and shall provide an accounting upon request to me or my legal representative.</p>

<p><strong>Exoneration.</strong> My Agent shall not be liable for any act done or omitted in good faith under this Power of Attorney, even if such act or omission results in a loss to my estate.</p>

<p><strong>Third-Party Reliance.</strong> Any third party who receives a copy of this Power of Attorney may rely upon it and shall incur no liability for any action taken in good faith reliance on this instrument. This provision is enforceable pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.9.</p>

<p><strong>Severability.</strong> If any provision of this Power of Attorney is held to be invalid, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.</p>

<p><strong>Revocation of Prior Powers.</strong> I hereby revoke all prior powers of attorney previously executed by me for the management of my financial and property affairs.</p>

<p><strong>Governing Law.</strong> This Power of Attorney shall be governed by the laws of the State of New Jersey.</p>

<h2>EXECUTION</h2>

<p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, I have executed this Durable General Power of Attorney on this ______ day of ______________, 20___, at {{personalInfo.city}}, {{personalInfo.county}} County, New Jersey.</p>

